}}

==Enemy==
This enemy is extremely strong. His reach exceeds that of more common variants, and he constantly does moderate damage to whatever he hits, with massive health and only one knockback. On top of that, he evades every meaningful status effect that can hold him back. Fortunately, he is even slower than the original, and his damage is somewhat underwhelming, requiring two hits to kill a [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and three for a level 20+86 [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]].

==Strategy==
As mentioned before, this enemy poses a huge threat. He can already push very far on his own, and in company of other threats becomes an extremely dangerous source of support. It is nigh-impossible to impede or snipe Papaou, forcing one to rely on the likes of [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] or [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] just to simply delay him while other units hopefully remove other threats for him to become manageable. One of the few working options to push him back is [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]], which can force him to flinch. The [[Cat Cannon]] will not work because of his [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]].

With that said, Papaou still has his counters:
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] is an effective meatshield due to its low cost, resistance to Traitless enemies and Behemoth Slayer. The dodge chance is low, but also helps against other Behemoths if it does activate, notably Traitless ones like [[Wild Doge]].
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] is an incredible tank when Papaou has minimal support for the same reasons as Haniwa. At just level 30, Reborn Warrior Doguemon can wall Papaou incredibly well and deal immense damage. However, this unit does not perform well outside of its niche, and being a mid-ranged tank, he may not be able to protect your other units.
*[[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]] has great stats against Traitless Behemoths, being able to tank many of Papaou's hits and deal hefty amounts of DPS, similarly to Doguemon.
*[[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]]' Behemoth Slayer and range advantage allows for great damage to all Behemoths, which adds up over time. Make sure the enemies don't push far, as Urs is relatively fragile and only outranges this enemy by 40, despite their Behemoth Slayer giving them a 30% dodge chance vs all Behemoths.

