==Trivia==
*[[wikipedia:Elephantidae|Elephantidae]] is a family of mammals that includes elephants and mammoths.
*The name Papaou (パパオウ) may be derived from ''papa'' (a childish way to say father), ぱおーん ''paōn'' (the Japanese onomatopoeia for an elephant's cry) and 王 ''ō'' (king). The ''papa'' part may be intended to complement [[Le'Solar]], whose Japanese name is ハハパオン ''Hahapaon'' (母 ''haha'' meaning mother).
*According to his Japanese description, Elephantidae Papaou is a [https://japantoday.com/category/features/lifestyle/from-carnivores-to-herbivores-how-men-are-defined-in-japan carnivorous man] - a man who actively approaches and seduces women, in stark contrast to the unassertive and less aggressive [[wikipedia:Herbivore men|herbivore men]]. Carnivorous men tend to have good communication skills, but Papaou seems to be an exception.
*As a fur-coated [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] elephant, Elephantidae Papaou could potentially represent [[wikia:monsterhunter:Gammoth|Gammoth]] from the ''Monster Hunter'' franchise; his Japanese description says that he aggressively pursues females, and Capcom has [https://twitter.com/CAPCOM_MHB/status/698476971710242816 stated] that all Gammoth found in-game are female, meaning Papaou could potentially represent the idea of an unseen male Gammoth. His white coloration suggests that it is [[wikia:monsterhunter:Elderfrost Gammoth|Elderfrost Gammoth]] being referenced in particular.
**He could also represent [[wikia:monsterhunter:Popo|Popo]], since he has a somewhat similar name and both have tusks and thick fur.
***Incidentally, during early development of ''Monster Hunter Generations'', [https://youtu.be/dF3F8cP5k1g Gammoth's model] was just an enlarged Popo with an added trunk.
*Prior to [[Version 12.4 Update|Version 12.4]], Elephantidae Papaou's foreswing was visibly desynced from his attack animation, as he attacked on frame 8 but his trunk hit the ground on frame 12.

